Evaluate and build derivation(s).

With no arguments: builds the default package from the compatibility-named crunch.ncl package root. With a .ncl file: builds derivations from that file. With .#name: builds a named output from the compatibility-named crunch.ncl package root.

Usage: mantle build [OPTIONS] [FILE]

Arguments:
  [FILE]
          Path to a .ncl file, or .#name selector, or omit for project default

Options:
  -I, --import-path <IMPORT_PATHS>
          Additional import paths for Nickel

  -v, --verbose
          Enable verbose logging

      --fix
          Auto-fix FOD hash mismatches by rewriting the .ncl source

      --log-level <LOG_LEVEL>
          Log level (trace, debug, info, warn, error)

      --json
          Emit errors as JSON objects for tooling integration

      --plan
          Show planned per-root actions without building or mutating local store state

      --offline-source-preflight
          Require imported source state for selected roots before planning or building

      --store <STORE>
          Where to export final build outputs on disk. Intermediate deps stay in castore. Source inputs always come from /nix/store. If not writable, builds still succeed (outputs in castore)
          
          [default: /nix/store]

      --evaluation-stream
          Emit the bounded mantle-evaluation-stream-v1 NDJSON contract on stdout

      --store-prefix <STORE_PREFIX>
          Logical store path prefix for derivation hashes. All output paths and ATerm hashes are computed against this prefix. Default: /mantle/store. Use --nix-compat for /nix/store
          
          [default: /mantle/store]

  -j, --jobs <JOBS>
          Maximum number of concurrent builds (default: CPU count, max 16)

      --nix-compat
          Shorthand for --store-prefix=/nix/store. For interop testing with Nix-computed derivations

      --state-dir <STATE_DIR>
          State directory for pathinfo.redb, blobs, and logs. Default: legacy $CRUNCH_STATE_DIR or $XDG_STATE_HOME/crunch or ~/.local/state/crunch. Use --state-dir for an explicit Mantle path

      --substituters <SUBSTITUTERS>
          Binary cache URLs for substitution (comma-separated)
          
          [default: https://cache.nixos.org]

      --base-store <BASE_STORES>
          Ordered list of read-only base store state directories for overlay composition. Declared in priority order (base A before base B)

      --no-substitute
          Disable remote binary cache substitution

      --signing-key <SIGNING_KEY>
          Path to a Nix-format ed25519 signing keypair file. If omitted, auto-generates one at $CRUNCH_CONFIG_DIR/signing-key

      --trusted-public-keys <TRUSTED_PUBLIC_KEYS>
          Trusted public keys for signature verification (name:base64). Overrides the default set (which includes cache.nixos.org-1)

      --trust-unsigned
          Accept unsigned/unverified PathInfo on cache hits. Escape hatch for migrating from unsigned stores

      --strict-hermetic
          Reject degraded hermetic behavior once strict-mode blockers exist

      --impure
          Permit ambient host dependencies; outputs are not proof-eligible

      --builder <BUILDER>
          Remote builder endpoint id for stdio remote-build dispatch

      --ticket-fd <TICKET_FD>
          Caller-owned non-terminal descriptor that provides one bearer credential

      --builder-program <BUILDER_PROGRAM>
          Program to spawn for stdio remote-build dispatch. Defaults to this mantle binary

      --builder-arg <BUILDER_ARGS>
          Argument passed to --builder-program; repeat to pass multiple arguments

      --trusted-builder-key <TRUSTED_BUILDER_KEYS>
          Trusted remote builder signing key name; repeat for multiple keys

      --remote-secret-manifest <REMOTE_SECRET_MANIFEST>
          SecretSpec metadata manifest for the local remote service
          
          [default: secretspec.toml]

      --remote-secret-profile <REMOTE_SECRET_PROFILE>
          Explicit SecretSpec profile for the local remote service
          
          [default: production]

      --remote-secret-provider <REMOTE_SECRET_PROVIDER>
          Explicit bounded SecretSpec provider for the local remote service
          
          [default: systemd-credential://]

      --remote-build-time-secs <REMOTE_BUILD_TIME_SECS>
          Remote request build-time limit in seconds
          
          [default: 3600]

      --remote-delta
          Offer bounded delta transfer with full-NAR streaming fallback to the remote builder

      --remote-observability-config <REMOTE_OBSERVABILITY_CONFIG>
          Typed Nickel configuration for disabled-by-default remote telemetry and trace propagation

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
